## asks what the program does, finds it vague, shares her situation, asks how it differs from reading online, then about the levels

Lead: what does your program actually do?

Sonia: My method is DETOX, NOURISH and FLOW. We find what in your daily life may be getting in the way, work out what your body needs, and build a way of living that supports your fertility and fits your real life. The Fertility Solution takes you through 16 modules over 6 months.

Lead: that sounds a bit vague tbh. what would you actually do with me?

Sonia: Fair. You send me your tracker information and I review it daily, your meal plan is built around you, and between our private sessions you text me what's happening and I help you adjust.

Lead: 36, pcos, trying 18 months naturally

Sonia: With PCOS, DETOX often starts with what's pushing your blood sugar the wrong way, NOURISH is what your body needs with PCOS, and FLOW is making it stick in your actual days, instead of another PCOS diet.

Lead: still not sure how that's different from reading stuff online

Sonia: Online can't see you. With PCOS the hard part is knowing which changes matter for your blood sugar and cycles, and whether they're working. That's what the daily review and texting are for: you send me what's happening and I tell you what to adjust.

Lead: on group could i still get a meal plan made for me?

Sonia: No, the personalized meal plan is part of Full. On Group you'd have the Eat Well module with hundreds of recipes, and the live sessions twice a week to bring your questions to.

Lead: ok. which one would you put me on?

Sonia: That depends on how much support you want. Would you rather work through it with the group around you, or have me looking at what you send and adjusting things with you day to day?
